* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.img binary
*.psbt binary
*.txn binary

# Published vector files are pinned by the hash of their bytes as upstream
# ships them. bip-0340/test-vectors.csv has CRLF line endings, and the rule
# above would store it with LF, so a fresh checkout would hash differently
# from both the pin in sign.spec.yaml and the file in bitcoin/bips.
spec/vectors/bip340-test-vectors.csv -text

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs so lockfile churn does not bury a real change.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

# MANIFEST.lock is generated by `make manifest` and is one line per source file.
# Deliberately NOT listed here. It carried `-diff`, directly under a comment
# saying a change in it is exactly what a reviewer must look at, and `-diff` is
# what makes git print "Binary files differ" instead of the changed lines. So
# every commit that moved a hash showed a reviewer nothing, on the one file in
# this repository whose entire purpose is to be compared by hand.
